  "title": "Labelled composition for the surviving one-bit decorations",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "A decoration s forces the pinwheel if (a) in every arc-consistent level-one collar the central tile's children can carry only s(0) or s(1) when their labelled collars lie in s's law, and (b) every labelled level-one collar whose decorated cut is legal and which survives arc consistency is itself in the law: then composition is forced at every level. For each of the nine one-bit decorations (up to exchanging labels) that exclude the rhombus and brick crystals, (a) holds and (b) fails at the pairwise level: 30 to 250 non-key and 50 to 125 key labelled level-one collars outside the law survive. One of the nine, s(0) = 10001, s(1) = 01100, with its relabelling, admits a brick-row crystal with period-4 diagonals after three cuts; the other eight admit none of those 16 crystals within three cuts on tori of index 1 or 2.",
